  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Approaching from the right, we have $x>-4,$ so we use the expression $f(x)={x}^{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {(-4)}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {(-4)}^{+}}{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={(-4)}^{2} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
